question_stem:
A block is pulled by a force $X$ in a straight line along a rough horizontal surface, as shown in Fig. 3.1.
{{figure:9702_s23_22_q03_figure_3_1}}
Assume that the total resistive force opposing the motion of the block is $0.80\text{ N}$ at all speeds of the block.
The variation with time $t$ of the magnitude of the force $X$ is shown in Fig. 3.2.
{{figure:9702_s23_22_q03_figure_3_2}}

parts.text:
The block is at rest at time $t = 0$.
On Fig. 3.3, sketch a graph to show the variation of the momentum of the block with time $t$ from $t = 0$ to $t = 6.0\text{ s}$. Numerical values of momentum are not required.
{{figure:9702_s23_22_q03_figure_3_3}}
